# Asset Naming Conventions

All assets live under `game/assets/` in subfolders by type.

## Backgrounds -- `game/assets/backgrounds/`

- Format: `bg-{number}.png`
- Sequential numbering matching scene order: `bg-1.png`, `bg-2.png`, ... `bg-22.png`
- Sub-scenes use a dash suffix: `bg-1-5.png` (stairwell between scene 1 and 2)
- Ending variants use a letter suffix: `bg-20a.png`, `bg-20b.png`, `bg-20c.png`
- Always `.png`

## Characters -- `game/assets/characters/`

- Format: `{name}.png` -- lowercase, hyphenated if multi-word
- Current files: `hero-v2.png`, `mom.png`, `erma.png`, `jeff.png`
- Use version suffixes (`-v2`, `-v3`) only when replacing an existing character sprite
- Must match the `image` path in `config.json` character definitions

## Objects -- `game/assets/objects/`

- Format: `{descriptive-name}.png` -- lowercase, hyphenated
- Use state suffixes for variants of the same object: `mailbox-closed.png`, `mailbox-open.png`
- Use pose suffixes for character-like objects: `cat-sitting.png`, `cat-legup.png`, `cat-cleaning.png`
- Always `.png`

## UI -- `game/assets/ui/`

- Format: `{element-name}.png` -- lowercase, hyphenated
- State variants use suffixes: `button-normal.png`, `button-hover.png`
- Always `.png`

## Audio -- `game/assets/audio/`

- Background music: `music.mp3`
- If adding more tracks, use descriptive names: `music-town.mp3`, `music-ending.mp3`
- `.mp3` format

## General Rules

- All filenames lowercase
- Use hyphens (`-`) not underscores or spaces
- Always use `.png` for images, `.mp3` for audio
- When adding a new asset, place it in the correct subfolder
- Reference paths in scene JSON files relative to the `game/` folder: `"assets/backgrounds/bg-3.png"`
